<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs of Main Theorems</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Density of the target class). ‣ Assumptions on the target class ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof Sketch.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof proceeds in three steps.
First, by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Relaxed target class and closure equivalence). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we approximate a broader function class that relaxes
the smoothness requirements and the assumptions in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Target class constraint). ‣ Assumptions on the target class ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Second, Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Order-statistic in the relaxed class). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Smooth selector). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> show that by constructing appropriate <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can faithfully recover all information from the original input sequence with simple <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, the outer function
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> can be applied to approximate an arbitrary sequence-to-vector target within this class.
Together, these steps establish the result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Density of the target class). ‣ Assumptions on the target class ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Density of the target class). ‣ Assumptions on the target class ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we first establish a few auxiliary lemmas.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Relaxed target class and closure equivalence)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{D}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{D}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in  <a href="#S4.E9" title="In Mathematical Formulation ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> but with only <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\in C([0,1]^{d},[0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\in C([0,1]^{d},[0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., we drop ”unique minimizer”, ”pairwise distinct”and ”PD Hessian”.Set <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{d,T}:=\bigcup_{D\geq 1}\mathcal{F}_{D}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{d,T}:=\bigcup_{D\geq 1}\mathcal{F}_{D}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}:=\bigcup_{D\geq 1}\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{D}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}:=\bigcup_{D\geq 1}\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{D}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{F}^{d,T}}^{\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}}=\overline{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}}^{\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}}\quad\text{on }\mathcal{X}_{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">on </mtext><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{F}^{d,T}}^{\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}}=\overline{\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}}^{\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}}\quad\text{on }\mathcal{X}_{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{H}(X_{T})=\widetilde{F}_{0}\!\big(\widetilde{z}_{1}(X_{T}),\dots,\widetilde{z}_{D}(X_{T})\big)\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{D}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{H}(X_{T})=\widetilde{F}_{0}\!\big(\widetilde{z}_{1}(X_{T}),\dots,\widetilde{z}_{D}(X_{T})\big)\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}_{D}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})=\min_{t\in S_{i}}\widetilde{f}_{i}(x(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})=\min_{t\in S_{i}}\widetilde{f}_{i}(x(t))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{f}_{i}\in C([0,1]^{d},[0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{f}_{i}\in C([0,1]^{d},[0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will construct <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{F}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{F}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Firstly, by Stone–Weierstrass, choose <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in C^{\infty}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in C^{\infty}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> so that
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> will be fixed later.
Because the uniform approximation can slightly leave <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, compose with a smooth strictly increasing squashing <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s:[-c,1+c]\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s:[-c,1+c]\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(u)=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(u)=u</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\circ p_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\circ p_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (for small enough <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), and replace <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\circ p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\circ p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We still write <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and retain <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq 2\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq 2\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Secondly, let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}\in\arg\min_{x\in[0,1]^{d}}p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}\in\arg\min_{x\in[0,1]^{d}}p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> (nonempty by compactness).
Pick <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,\tfrac{1}{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,\tfrac{1}{4})</annotation></semantics></math> small and a <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> bump <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> supported in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\xi_{i},2r)\cap[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\xi_{i},2r)\cap[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and with
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">negative definite</em>.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                      
                      
                      
                    For instance take <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(x)=\psi(\|x-\xi_{i}\|^{2}/r^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(x)=\psi(\|x-\xi_{i}\|^{2}/r^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="footnote1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="footnote1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="footnote1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="footnote1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>; then <math id="footnote1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})\prec 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≺</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})\prec 0</annotation></semantics></math> and its norm scales like <math id="footnote1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
Define, for parameters <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i,1},\delta_{i,2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i,1},\delta_{i,2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> to be fixed,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(x)\ :=\ p_{i}(x)\;-\;\delta_{i,1}\,\phi_{i}(x)\;+\;\delta_{i,2}\,\phi_{i}(x)\,\|x-\xi_{i}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(x)\ :=\ p_{i}(x)\;-\;\delta_{i,1}\,\phi_{i}(x)\;+\;\delta_{i,2}\,\phi_{i}(x)\,\|x-\xi_{i}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">(i) Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(\xi_{i})=p_{i}(\xi_{i})-\delta_{i,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(\xi_{i})=p_{i}(\xi_{i})-\delta_{i,1}</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(x)\geq p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(x)\geq p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(x)&gt;p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(x)&gt;p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(\xi_{i},2r)\setminus\{\xi_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(\xi_{i},2r)\setminus\{\xi_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique global minimizer</em> of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(ii) At <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}g_{i}(\xi_{i})=\nabla^{2}p_{i}(\xi_{i})\;-\;\delta_{i,1}\,\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})\;+\;2\delta_{i,2}I." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}g_{i}(\xi_{i})=\nabla^{2}p_{i}(\xi_{i})\;-\;\delta_{i,1}\,\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})\;+\;2\delta_{i,2}I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so choosing <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\delta_{i,1},\delta_{i,2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\delta_{i,1},\delta_{i,2})</annotation></semantics></math> suitably makes <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}g_{i}(\xi_{i})\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}g_{i}(\xi_{i})\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> (PD).
Because <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,\|x-\xi_{i}\|^{2}\|_{\infty}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,\|x-\xi_{i}\|^{2}\|_{\infty}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\delta_{i,1}\;+\;\delta_{i,2}\,(2r)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\delta_{i,1}\;+\;\delta_{i,2}\,(2r)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, by taking <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> small and then <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i,1},\delta_{i,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i,1},\delta_{i,2}</annotation></semantics></math> small (using the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> scaling in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\phi_{i}(\xi_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> to keep the Hessian PD), we can ensure both PD at <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thirdly, we use tiny translation to remove distinctiveness. It may happen that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}=\xi_{i^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}=\xi_{i^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq i^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq i^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose pairwise distinct small vectors <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and fix a smooth cutoff
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in C^{\infty}([0,1]^{d},[0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in C^{\infty}([0,1]^{d},[0,1])</annotation></semantics></math> that equals <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r,1-r]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r,1-r]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and vanishes near the boundary.
Define a <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> diffeomorphism of the cube,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}(x)\ :=\ x\;-\;\varepsilon_{i}\,\chi(x)\,v_{i},\qquad\text{with }\varepsilon_{i}&gt;0\text{ small}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> small</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}(x)\ :=\ x\;-\;\varepsilon_{i}\,\chi(x)\,v_{i},\qquad\text{with }\varepsilon_{i}&gt;0\text{ small}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrarily close to the identity in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for small <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, maps <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to itself, and
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}:=g_{i}\circ\Phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}:=g_{i}\circ\Phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> has a (unique) minimizer at <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}:=\Phi_{i}^{-1}(\xi_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}:=\Phi_{i}^{-1}(\xi_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For different <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, these points are distinct if the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are distinct and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are small but nonzero.
Moreover, because <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla g_{i}(\xi_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla g_{i}(\xi_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the Hessian at <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}h_{i}(x^{(i)})\;=\;D\Phi_{i}(x^{(i)})^{\!\top}\,\nabla^{2}g_{i}(\xi_{i})\,D\Phi_{i}(x^{(i)})\;\succ\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}h_{i}(x^{(i)})\;=\;D\Phi_{i}(x^{(i)})^{\!\top}\,\nabla^{2}g_{i}(\xi_{i})\,D\Phi_{i}(x^{(i)})\;\succ\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">so PD is preserved.
Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz on the compact cube, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h_{i}-g_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq L_{i}\,\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h_{i}-g_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq L_{i}\,\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence by taking <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> small we get <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h_{i}-g_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h_{i}-g_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, if needed, compose with the same strictly increasing squashing <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as in Step 1 and set</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\ :=\ s\circ h_{i}\in C^{2}([0,1]^{d},[0,1])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\ :=\ s\circ h_{i}\in C^{2}([0,1]^{d},[0,1]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing, it preserves the minimizer location and, at the minimizer <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}(s\circ h_{i})(x^{(i)})=s^{\prime}\!\big(h_{i}(x^{(i)})\big)\,\nabla^{2}h_{i}(x^{(i)})\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}(s\circ h_{i})(x^{(i)})=s^{\prime}\!\big(h_{i}(x^{(i)})\big)\,\nabla^{2}h_{i}(x^{(i)})\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{i}-h_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{i}-h_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math> by construction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Collecting the bounds from previous deduction:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\underbrace{\|p_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq 2\eta}+\underbrace{\|g_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\eta}+\underbrace{\|h_{i}-g_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\eta}+\underbrace{\|f_{i}-h_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\eta}\;\leq\;5\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\underbrace{\|p_{i}-\widetilde{f}_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq 2\eta}+\underbrace{\|g_{i}-p_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\eta}+\underbrace{\|h_{i}-g_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\eta}+\underbrace{\|f_{i}-h_{i}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\eta}\;\leq\;5\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto\min_{t\in S_{i}}u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto\min_{t\in S_{i}}u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence the corresponding features
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{z}_{i}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(x(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{z}_{i}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(x(t))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{z}_{i}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S_{i}}\widetilde{f}_{i}(x(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{z}_{i}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S_{i}}\widetilde{f}_{i}(x(t))</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{z}_{i}-\widetilde{z}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq 5\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{z}_{i}-\widetilde{z}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq 5\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\widetilde{F}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\widetilde{F}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a modulus of continuity of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> so small that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\widetilde{F}_{0}}(5\eta)\leq\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\widetilde{F}_{0}}(5\eta)\leq\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\widetilde{F}_{0}\big(\bar{z}(X_{T})\big)-\widetilde{F}_{0}\big(\widetilde{z}(X_{T})\big)\big\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon/2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\widetilde{F}_{0}\big(\bar{z}(X_{T})\big)-\widetilde{F}_{0}\big(\widetilde{z}(X_{T})\big)\big\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon/2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, approximate <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> by some <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}\in C^{1}([0,1]^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}\in C^{1}([0,1]^{D})</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math> (Stone–Weierstrass). Setting</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(X_{T})\ :=\ F_{0}\big(\bar{z}_{1}(X_{T}),\ldots,\bar{z}_{D}(X_{T})\big)\in\mathcal{F}^{d,T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(X_{T})\ :=\ F_{0}\big(\bar{z}_{1}(X_{T}),\ldots,\bar{z}_{D}(X_{T})\big)\in\mathcal{F}^{d,T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\ \leq\ \underbrace{\|F_{0}(\bar{z})-\widetilde{F}_{0}(\bar{z})\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/2}+\underbrace{\|\widetilde{F}_{0}(z)-\widetilde{F}_{0}(\widetilde{z})\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/2}\ \leq\ \varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\ \leq\ \underbrace{\|F_{0}(\bar{z})-\widetilde{F}_{0}(\bar{z})\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/2}+\underbrace{\|\widetilde{F}_{0}(z)-\widetilde{F}_{0}(\widetilde{z})\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/2}\ \leq\ \varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">This shows <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}\subset\overline{\mathcal{F}^{d,T}}^{\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}\subset\overline{\mathcal{F}^{d,T}}^{\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The reverse inclusion is simple, hence we have the lemma.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we now focus on the relaxed class <math id="Thmremarkx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Relaxed target class and closure equivalence). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lifts the result to the original class <math id="Thmremarkx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Order-statistic in the relaxed class)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Without loss of generation, suppose <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4|T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4|T</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\frac{T}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\frac{T}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}=\{x(1),\dots,x(T)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}=\{x(1),\dots,x(T)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}(X_{T}):=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}B\subseteq[T]\\
|B|=m\end{subarray}}\ \min_{u\in B}x(u)_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}(X_{T}):=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}B\subseteq[T]\\
|B|=m\end{subarray}}\ \min_{u\in B}x(u)_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and for each fixed <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}(X_{T}):=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}A\subseteq[T]\\
|A|=m,\ t\in A\end{subarray}}\ \min_{u\in A}x(u)_{j},\qquad Z_{t,j}(X_{T}):=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}A\subseteq[T]\\
|A|=m,\ t\in A\end{subarray}}\ \min_{u\in A}(1-x(u)_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}(X_{T}):=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}A\subseteq[T]\\
|A|=m,\ t\in A\end{subarray}}\ \min_{u\in A}x(u)_{j},\qquad Z_{t,j}(X_{T}):=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}A\subseteq[T]\\
|A|=m,\ t\in A\end{subarray}}\ \min_{u\in A}(1-x(u)_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1,j}\geq\cdots\geq v_{T,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1,j}\geq\cdots\geq v_{T,j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sorted values of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x(1)_{j},\dots,x(T)_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x(1)_{j},\dots,x(T)_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}=v_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}=v_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the multi-set <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x(u)_{j}:u\in[T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x(u)_{j}:u\in[T]\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1,j}\geq\cdots\geq v_{T,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1,j}\geq\cdots\geq v_{T,j}</annotation></semantics></math> (nonincreasing) and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1,j}\leq\cdots\leq w_{T,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1,j}\leq\cdots\leq w_{T,j}</annotation></semantics></math> (nondecreasing). Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}=\min\{x(t)_{j},\ v_{m,j}\},\qquad 1-Z_{t,j}=\max\{x(t)_{j},\ w_{m,j}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}=\min\{x(t)_{j},\ v_{m,j}\},\qquad 1-Z_{t,j}=\max\{x(t)_{j},\ w_{m,j}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)_{j}\leq v_{m,j}\ \Rightarrow\ Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j},\qquad x(t)_{j}\geq w_{m,j}\ \Rightarrow\ 1-Z_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)_{j}\leq v_{m,j}\ \Rightarrow\ Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j},\qquad x(t)_{j}\geq w_{m,j}\ \Rightarrow\ 1-Z_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Among all <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-subsets <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{u\in B}x(u)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{u\in B}x(u)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is attained by picking the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> largest coordinates, so <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}=v_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}=v_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Forcing <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, the choice of the other <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> indices to maximize the minimum is the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> largest among <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x(u)_{j}:u\neq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x(u)_{j}:u\neq t\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}=\min\{x(t)_{j},v_{m,j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}=\min\{x(t)_{j},v_{m,j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, note that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{u\in A}(1-x(u)_{j})=1-\max_{u\in A}x(u)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{u\in A}(1-x(u)_{j})=1-\max_{u\in A}x(u)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, so maximizing it over <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as minimizing <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{u\in A}x(u)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{u\in A}x(u)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, which picks <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> plus the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m\!-\!1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m\!-\!1)</annotation></semantics></math> smallest leading to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-Z_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-Z_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The particular statements follow immediately.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smooth selector)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}\ :=\ \frac{e^{q(\,1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j}\,)^{2}}\,(1-Z_{t,j})+e^{q(\,Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j}\,)^{2}}\,Y_{t,j}}{e^{q(\,1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j}\,)^{2}}+e^{q(\,Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j}\,)^{2}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}\ :=\ \frac{e^{q(\,1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j}\,)^{2}}\,(1-Z_{t,j})+e^{q(\,Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j}\,)^{2}}\,Y_{t,j}}{e^{q(\,1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j}\,)^{2}}+e^{q(\,Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j}\,)^{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}\to x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}\to x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Order-statistic in the relaxed class). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, if <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)_{j}\geq U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)_{j}\geq U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}=v_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}=v_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j})^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j})^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-Z_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-Z_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j})^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j})^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the weight concentrates on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-Z_{t,j})=x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-Z_{t,j})=x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)_{j}\leq U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)_{j}\leq U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m,j}\geq x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m,j}\geq x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j})^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-Z_{t,j}-w_{m,j})^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j})^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{t,j}-v_{m,j})^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> concentrating on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m,j}\leq x(t)_{j}\leq U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m,j}\leq x(t)_{j}\leq U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-Z_{t,j}=Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-Z_{t,j}=Y_{t,j}=x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, so either of three settings leads to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The compactness of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> gives us the uniform property.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we begin our formal proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Density of the target class). ‣ Assumptions on the target class ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Relaxed target class and closure equivalence). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in C(\mathcal{X}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in C(\mathcal{X}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to construct an <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{H}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{H}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>, since the lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Relaxed target class and closure equivalence). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> could lift it to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> with another <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\frac{T}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\frac{T}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each coordinate <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and each <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq[T]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=m</annotation></semantics></math>, include the relaxed primitives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(j,S)}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S}x(t)_{j},\qquad\bar{z}^{(j,S)}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S}(1-x(t)_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(j,S)}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S}x(t)_{j},\qquad\bar{z}^{(j,S)}(X_{T}):=\min_{t\in S}(1-x(t)_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">To form the thresholds <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> needed in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Order-statistic in the relaxed class). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, additionally include:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{t\in S}x(t)_{j}\quad\text{for all }S\subseteq[T]\setminus\{t\}\text{ with }|S|=m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{t\in S}x(t)_{j}\quad\text{for all }S\subseteq[T]\setminus\{t\}\text{ with }|S|=m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{t\in S}(1-x(t)_{j})\quad\text{for all }S\subseteq[T]\setminus\{t\}\text{ with }|S|=T-m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{t\in S}(1-x(t)_{j})\quad\text{for all }S\subseteq[T]\setminus\{t\}\text{ with }|S|=T-m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using smooth log-sum-exp (softmax) in the outer function <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can recover the subset-wise maximum required to compute <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> from these primitives.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Smooth selector). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> there exists <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{X_{T}\in\mathcal{X}_{T}}\max_{t\in[T],\,j\in[d]}\big|\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}-x(t)_{j}\big|\ \leq\ \delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{X_{T}\in\mathcal{X}_{T}}\max_{t\in[T],\,j\in[d]}\big|\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}-x(t)_{j}\big|\ \leq\ \delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">By uniform continuity of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> on the compact <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> so that this implies <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F(X_{T})-F(\widehat{X}_{q}(T))|\leq\varepsilon/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F(X_{T})-F(\widehat{X}_{q}(T))|\leq\varepsilon/4</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}_{q}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}_{q}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> stacks the coordinates <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{x}_{q}(t)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. We approximate the continuous map <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto F(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto F(u)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{dT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{dT}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly by a polynomial <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon/4</annotation></semantics></math> (Stone–Weierstrass). Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{H}(X_{T}):=\big(P\circ\mathrm{vec}\big)(\widehat{X}_{q}(T))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>vec</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{H}(X_{T}):=\big(P\circ\mathrm{vec}\big)(\widehat{X}_{q}(T)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is a <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> function of the inner features. Hence <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{H}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{H}\in\widetilde{\mathcal{F}}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\leq\underbrace{\|F-F\circ\widehat{X}_{q}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/4}+\underbrace{\|F\circ\widehat{X}_{q}-P\circ\widehat{X}_{q}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/4}\leq\varepsilon/2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F-\widetilde{H}\|_{\infty}\leq\underbrace{\|F-F\circ\widehat{X}_{q}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/4}+\underbrace{\|F\circ\widehat{X}_{q}-P\circ\widehat{X}_{q}\|_{\infty}}_{\leq\varepsilon/4}\leq\varepsilon/2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Relaxed target class and closure equivalence). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to replace each relaxed primitives by admissible <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> functions with unique minimizers
and to replace <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> by function <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> so that the final error increases by at most <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
This leads to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}_{D}^{d,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}_{D}^{d,T}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F-f\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F-f\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i1" title="item 2 (1) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (1)</span></a> </h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we prove Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i1" title="item 2 (1) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (1)</span></a></p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof Sketch.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The idea is straightforward. Each attention head is assigned to approximate one term
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(x(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(x(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. Once these components are extracted, the outer function
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> can be approximated by a suitable <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i1" title="item 2 (1) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (1)</span></a>: Sufficient expressivity with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> heads.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be given.
Throughout the proof, constants depending only on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,D,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,D,T)</annotation></semantics></math> are absorbed into
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d,D,T}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d,D,T}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> which may change from line to line.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the display equation <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Transformer Hypothesis Class ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, each head produces an <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vector and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Concat}_{i=1}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Concat</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Concat}_{i=1}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> gives a vector in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{nh}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{nh}</annotation></semantics></math> before <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the construction, we realize the usual <em id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">block-by-head</em> parameterization, which means that
the encoder outputs a block-decomposed embedding</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}(t)\;=\;\bigl(\hat{x}^{(1)}(t),\ldots,\hat{x}^{(D)}(t)\bigr)\in\mathbb{R}^{2D},\qquad\hat{x}^{(i)}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}(t)\;=\;\bigl(\hat{x}^{(1)}(t),\ldots,\hat{x}^{(D)}(t)\bigr)\in\mathbb{R}^{2D},\qquad\hat{x}^{(i)}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th head only reads the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th block via block-diagonal
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q,i},W_{V,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q,i},W_{V,i}</annotation></semantics></math> (entries bounded by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>).
This keeps the parameter counts within the same order. We therefore set the <em id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per-head
embedding dimension</em> to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Firstly, from Assumption (A2), for any <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> there exist two-layer FFNs
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,\delta}:[0,1]^{d}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,\delta}:[0,1]^{d}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{x\in[0,1]^{d}}\,|f_{i}(x)-\Psi_{i,\delta}(x)|\leq\delta,\qquad\mathrm{width}(\Psi_{i,\delta})\leq\frac{C_{2}}{\delta^{\gamma_{f}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>width</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{x\in[0,1]^{d}}\,|f_{i}(x)-\Psi_{i,\delta}(x)|\leq\delta,\qquad\mathrm{width}(\Psi_{i,\delta})\leq\frac{C_{2}}{\delta^{\gamma_{f}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{f}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{f}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the exponent from (A2).
Define for each head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the position gate</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(s):=\begin{cases}0,&amp;s\in S_{i},\\[2.0pt]
-1,&amp;s\notin S_{i},\end{cases}\qquad s\in[T]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(s):=\begin{cases}0,&amp;s\in S_{i},\\[2.0pt]
-1,&amp;s\notin S_{i},\end{cases}\qquad s\in[T].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">(Recall <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}\subset[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}\subset[T]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{i}|\geq\alpha T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{i}|\geq\alpha T</annotation></semantics></math> by equation <a href="#S4.E8" title="In Mathematical Formulation ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.)
We implement the encoder <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> so that its <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th block is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}^{(i)}(t)\;=\;\bigl(\,\Psi_{i,\delta}(x(t))\,,\,r_{i}(t)\,\bigr)\in[0,1]\times\{-1,0\}\subset[-1,1]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}^{(i)}(t)\;=\;\bigl(\,\Psi_{i,\delta}(x(t))\,,\,r_{i}(t)\,\bigr)\in[0,1]\times\{-1,0\}\subset[-1,1]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">This choice follows <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{x}(t)\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{2D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{x}(t)\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{2D}</annotation></semantics></math>. After a fixed rescaling (absorbed into <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>), this meets the norm constraint.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Secondly, we would like to use head-wise attention to isolate the minimum on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we take a single attention logit (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{h}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{h}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) by choosing</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{O,i}=I,\qquad W_{K,i}=\begin{bmatrix}-1&amp;\;1\end{bmatrix},\qquad W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0}=1,\qquad W_{V,i}=I_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn> 1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{O,i}=I,\qquad W_{K,i}=\begin{bmatrix}-1&amp;\;1\end{bmatrix},\qquad W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0}=1,\qquad W_{V,i}=I_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">All entries are within the allowed bound <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. With the block equation <a href="#A1.E11" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, the (pre-softmax) score of token <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}(t)\;=\;(W_{K,i}\hat{x}^{(i)}(t))^{\top}(W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0})\;=\;-\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)+r_{i}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}(t)\;=\;(W_{K,i}\hat{x}^{(i)}(t))^{\top}(W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0})\;=\;-\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)+r_{i}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma[\rho_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma[\rho_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> be the softmax equation <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Transformer Hypothesis Class ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the head-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> value readout (first coordinate of the head output)</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})\;:=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)\;\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})\;:=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)\;\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the second coordinate is unused. <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math> could ignore it via a fixed linear projection,
counted in the constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d,D,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d,D,T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we give a uniform bound on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}:=\Psi_{i,\delta}(x(t))\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}:=\Psi_{i,\delta}(x(t))\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and split the sum into <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. From <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(t)=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(t)=-1</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)=\frac{e^{\beta(-a_{t}+r_{i}(t))}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}+\sum_{u\in S_{i}^{c}}e^{-\beta(a_{u}+1)}}\leq\begin{cases}\displaystyle\frac{e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}},&amp;t\in S_{i},\\[10.0pt]
e^{-\beta}\cdot\displaystyle\frac{e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}},&amp;t\in S_{i}^{c}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)=\frac{e^{\beta(-a_{t}+r_{i}(t))}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}+\sum_{u\in S_{i}^{c}}e^{-\beta(a_{u}+1)}}\leq\begin{cases}\displaystyle\frac{e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}},&amp;t\in S_{i},\\[10.0pt]
e^{-\beta}\cdot\displaystyle\frac{e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}},&amp;t\in S_{i}^{c}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}_{i}=\sum_{t\in S_{i}}\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)a_{t}+\sum_{t\in S_{i}^{c}}\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)a_{t}\leq\underbrace{\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}}_{\text{Gibbs mean on }S_{i}}\;+\;e^{-\beta}\,\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}^{c}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Gibbs mean on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}_{i}=\sum_{t\in S_{i}}\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)a_{t}+\sum_{t\in S_{i}^{c}}\sigma[\rho_{i}](t)a_{t}\leq\underbrace{\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}}_{\text{Gibbs mean on }S_{i}}\;+\;e^{-\beta}\,\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}^{c}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">To simplify, we denote <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{*}:=\min_{t\in S_{i}}a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{*}:=\min_{t\in S_{i}}a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}:=a_{t}-a_{*}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}:=a_{t}-a_{*}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}=a_{*}+\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}}b_{t}e^{-\beta b_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta b_{u}}}\;\leq\;a_{*}+\sum_{t\in S_{i}}b_{t}e^{-\beta b_{t}}\;\leq\;a_{*}+\frac{|S_{i}|-1}{e\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}=a_{*}+\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}}b_{t}e^{-\beta b_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta b_{u}}}\;\leq\;a_{*}+\sum_{t\in S_{i}}b_{t}e^{-\beta b_{t}}\;\leq\;a_{*}+\frac{|S_{i}|-1}{e\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">The inequality comes from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{b\in[0,1]}be^{-\beta b}=e^{-1}/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{b\in[0,1]}be^{-\beta b}=e^{-1}/\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and one of the
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the denominator in the middle fraction is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. For the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> term in <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>,
we use <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> to get</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-\beta}\,\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}^{c}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}\;\leq\;e^{-\beta}\,\bigl|S_{i}^{c}\bigr|\;\leq\;e^{-\beta}\,T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\beta}\,\frac{\sum_{t\in S_{i}^{c}}a_{t}e^{-\beta a_{t}}}{\sum_{u\in S_{i}}e^{-\beta a_{u}}}\;\leq\;e^{-\beta}\,\bigl|S_{i}^{c}\bigr|\;\leq\;e^{-\beta}\,T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two bounds, we have the uniform estimate:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\;\leq\;\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})\;\leq\;\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\;+\;\frac{|S_{i}|-1}{e\beta}+Te^{-\beta}\qquad(\beta\geq 1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\;\leq\;\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})\;\leq\;\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\;+\;\frac{|S_{i}|-1}{e\beta}+Te^{-\beta}\qquad(\beta\geq 1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{i}|\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{i}|\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\;\leq\;\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})-\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\;\leq\;C_{T}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\beta}+e^{-\beta}\Bigr),\qquad C_{T}:=\max\{T/e,\;T\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\;\leq\;\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})-\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\;\leq\;C_{T}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\beta}+e^{-\beta}\Bigr),\qquad C_{T}:=\max\{T/e,\;T\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thirdly, we need to lift bounds from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. From  equation <a href="#A1.E10" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|\min_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)-\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\Bigr|\;\leq\;\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\min_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)-\min_{t\in S_{i}}\Psi_{i,\delta}\bigl(x(t)\bigr)\Bigr|\;\leq\;\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Together with equation <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})-\bar{z}_{i}(X_{T})\bigr|\;\leq\;\delta+C_{T}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\beta}+e^{-\beta}\Bigr)\qquad\text{for all }X_{T}\in\mathcal{X}_{T},\ i=1,\dots,D." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\tilde{z}_{i}(X_{T})-\bar{z}_{i}(X_{T})\bigr|\;\leq\;\delta+C_{T}\Bigl(\frac{1}{\beta}+e^{-\beta}\Bigr)\qquad\text{for all }X_{T}\in\mathcal{X}_{T},\ i=1,\dots,D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}:=\sup_{z\in[0,1]^{D}}\|\nabla F_{0}(z)\|_{1}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}:=\sup_{z\in[0,1]^{D}}\|\nabla F_{0}(z)\|_{1}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (compactness and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Choose</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta:=\frac{\varepsilon}{4L_{0}D},\qquad\beta\geq\beta_{\varepsilon}:=\max\!\left\{1,\ \frac{4C_{T}L_{0}D}{\varepsilon},\ \log\!\Bigl(\frac{4C_{T}L_{0}D}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta:=\frac{\varepsilon}{4L_{0}D},\qquad\beta\geq\beta_{\varepsilon}:=\max\!\left\{1,\ \frac{4C_{T}L_{0}D}{\varepsilon},\ \log\!\Bigl(\frac{4C_{T}L_{0}D}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then by equation <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{z}(X_{T})-z(X_{T})\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\frac{\varepsilon}{2L_{0}D}\qquad\text{for all }X_{T}\in\mathcal{X}_{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{z}(X_{T})-z(X_{T})\|_{\infty}\;\leq\;\frac{\varepsilon}{2L_{0}D}\qquad\text{for all }X_{T}\in\mathcal{X}_{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we constrcut the approximation for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and count the number of parameter. By Assumption (A1), there exists a two-layer FFN <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\delta_{0}}:\,[0,1]^{D}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\delta_{0}}:\,[0,1]^{D}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>
with width <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq C_{1}/\delta_{0}^{\gamma_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq C_{1}/\delta_{0}^{\gamma_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (for some <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{z\in[0,1]^{D}}\,|F_{0}(z)-\Phi_{\delta_{0}}(z)|\leq\delta_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{z\in[0,1]^{D}}\,|F_{0}(z)-\Phi_{\delta_{0}}(z)|\leq\delta_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}:=\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}:=\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the model’s final feed-forward <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math> to project
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2D}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2D}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> by keeping the first coordinate of each head (a fixed linear
map with entries in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>) and apply <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\delta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\delta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|\hat{F}(\operatorname{Concat}_{i}(\cdot))-F_{0}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Concat</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|\hat{F}(\operatorname{Concat}_{i}(\cdot))-F_{0}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\bigl|\Phi_{\delta_{0}}\bigl(\tilde{z}(X_{T})\bigr)-\Phi_{\delta_{0}}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)\bigr|+\bigl|\Phi_{\delta_{0}}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)-F_{0}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\bigl|\Phi_{\delta_{0}}\bigl(\tilde{z}(X_{T})\bigr)-\Phi_{\delta_{0}}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)\bigr|+\bigl|\Phi_{\delta_{0}}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)-F_{0}\bigl(z(X_{T})\bigr)\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{0}\,\|\tilde{z}(X_{T})-z(X_{T})\|_{1}+\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{0}\,\|\tilde{z}(X_{T})-z(X_{T})\|_{1}+\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{0}D\,\|\tilde{z}(X_{T})-z(X_{T})\|_{\infty}+\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{0}D\,\|\tilde{z}(X_{T})-z(X_{T})\|_{\infty}+\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon/2+\varepsilon/2\;=\;\varepsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon/2+\varepsilon/2\;=\;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we used equation <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> in the last inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the trainable components are composed of three parts:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> subnetworks <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i,\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i,\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> inside the encoder blocks equation <a href="#A1.E11" title="In Proof of Theorem : Sufficient expressivity with D heads. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the fixed-size projections <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q,i},W_{K,i},W_{V,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q,i},W_{K,i},W_{V,i}</annotation></semantics></math> (size <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(D)</annotation></semantics></math> and independent of <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the two-layer FFN <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\delta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\delta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> used inside <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\;\leq\;C^{\prime}\,D\cdot\frac{1}{\delta^{\gamma_{f}}}\;+\;C^{\prime\prime}\cdot\frac{1}{\delta_{0}^{\gamma_{0}}}\;+\;C^{\prime\prime\prime}\qquad\text{for constants }C^{\prime},C^{\prime\prime},C^{\prime\prime\prime}=C_{d,D,T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for constants </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\;\leq\;C^{\prime}\,D\cdot\frac{1}{\delta^{\gamma_{f}}}\;+\;C^{\prime\prime}\cdot\frac{1}{\delta_{0}^{\gamma_{0}}}\;+\;C^{\prime\prime\prime}\qquad\text{for constants }C^{\prime},C^{\prime\prime},C^{\prime\prime\prime}=C_{d,D,T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">With <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\Theta(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\Theta(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=\Theta(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=\Theta(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> chosen above,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\;\leq\;\frac{C_{d,D,T}}{\varepsilon^{\gamma}},\qquad\gamma:=\max\{\gamma_{f},\gamma_{0}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\;\leq\;\frac{C_{d,D,T}}{\varepsilon^{\gamma}},\qquad\gamma:=\max\{\gamma_{f},\gamma_{0}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">and the construction uses <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=D</annotation></semantics></math> heads with per-head dimension <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> and achieves
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i1" title="item 2 (1) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (1)</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i2" title="item 2 (2) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (2)</span></a> </h4>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof Sketch.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The argument proceeds in two parts. The core idea is to construct two sequences whose
representations after the attention layer are indistinguishably close, on the order of
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\epsilon^{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\epsilon^{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, yet whose target outputs differ by at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> then implies the lower bound on the parameter count required for
approximation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>,
we obtain <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint neighborhoods around the minima <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D&gt;s=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D&gt;s=h</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists at least one neighborhood not selected by the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> heads.
Within this region, the pigeonhole principle guarantees the existence of two distinct
subsequences. By carefully designing these subsequences, we ensure that their outputs
after the attention layer are nearly indistinguishable, while their target values differ
by at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Extending them to full sequences completes the construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn to the full proof.
To establish Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i2" title="item 2 (2) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (2)</span></a>,
we begin by introducing several auxiliary lemmas that will serve as building blocks for the argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v_{1}-v_{2}\|_{2}\leq A\quad\text{and}\quad\|\hat{F}(v_{1})-\hat{F}(v_{2})\|\geq B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v_{1}-v_{2}\|_{2}\leq A\quad\text{and}\quad\|\hat{F}(v_{1})-\hat{F}(v_{2})\|\geq B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is a two-layer feed-forward network
satisfying the constraints stated above. Then <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math> must use at least</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\!\left(\frac{B}{A\sqrt{n}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.653em;" width="0.653em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\!\left(\frac{B}{A\sqrt{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">parameters.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x:=v_{1}-v_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x:=v_{1}-v_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta F:=\hat{F}(v_{1})-\hat{F}(v_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta F:=\hat{F}(v_{1})-\hat{F}(v_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose the two-layer network with width <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> be</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}(x)\;=\;V\,\sigma(Ux+b)+c," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}(x)\;=\;V\,\sigma(Ux+b)+c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz acting coordinate-wise and every entry of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,V,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,V,b,c</annotation></semantics></math> has magnitude at most <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th output coordinate, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta F_{j}=\sum_{r=1}^{p}V_{jr}\!\left(\sigma(u_{r}^{\top}v_{1}+b_{r})-\sigma(u_{r}^{\top}v_{2}+b_{r})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta F_{j}=\sum_{r=1}^{p}V_{jr}\!\left(\sigma(u_{r}^{\top}v_{1}+b_{r})-\sigma(u_{r}^{\top}v_{2}+b_{r})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz property of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and Cauchy–Schwarz inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta F_{j}|\leq\sum_{r=1}^{p}|V_{jr}|\,|u_{r}^{\top}\Delta x|\leq\sum_{r=1}^{p}|V_{jr}|\,\|u_{r}\|_{2}\,\|\Delta x\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta F_{j}|\leq\sum_{r=1}^{p}|V_{jr}|\,|u_{r}^{\top}\Delta x|\leq\sum_{r=1}^{p}|V_{jr}|\,\|u_{r}\|_{2}\,\|\Delta x\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the entrywise weight bound, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{r}\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{r}\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{jr}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{jr}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta F_{j}|\;\leq\;p\,\sqrt{n}\,\|\Delta x\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta F_{j}|\;\leq\;p\,\sqrt{n}\,\|\Delta x\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> be the norm used in the lemma statement. By norm equivalence in finite dimensions, there exists <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{m}\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{m}\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> depending only on the chosen norm and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y\|\leq\frac{1}{c_{m}}\|y\|_{\infty}\quad\text{for all }y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y\|\leq\frac{1}{c_{m}}\|y\|_{\infty}\quad\text{for all }y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta F\|\geq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta F\|\geq B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text"> implies <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta F\|_{\infty}\geq c_{m}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta F\|_{\infty}\geq c_{m}B</annotation></semantics></math>, so there is some <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta F_{j^{\star}}|\;\geq\;c_{m}B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta F_{j^{\star}}|\;\geq\;c_{m}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this with equation <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta x\|_{2}\leq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta x\|_{2}\leq A</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{m}B\;\leq\;p\,\sqrt{n}\,A\quad\Longrightarrow\quad p\;\geq\;\frac{c_{m}\,B}{A\sqrt{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{m}B\;\leq\;p\,\sqrt{n}\,A\quad\Longrightarrow\quad p\;\geq\;\frac{c_{m}\,B}{A\sqrt{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{eff}}\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{eff}}\leq p</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of hidden units that actually affect the output, i.e., those with a nonzero row in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and a nonzero entry in the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. The above bound holds with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{eff}}\geq c_{m}B/(A\sqrt{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{eff}}\geq c_{m}B/(A\sqrt{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Each such unit uses at least one nonzero parameter in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and one in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, so the parameter counts <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq p_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq p_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\;\geq\;\frac{c_{m}\,B}{A\sqrt{n}}\;=\;\Omega\!\left(\frac{B}{A\sqrt{n}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.653em;" width="0.653em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\;\geq\;\frac{c_{m}\,B}{A\sqrt{n}}\;=\;\Omega\!\left(\frac{B}{A\sqrt{n}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;R</annotation></semantics></math>,
there exist constants <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with the following property:
there exists a segment <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}\subset B(x^{(i)},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}\subset B(x^{(i)},r)</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{i}(x)-f_{i}(y)|\;\geq\;L_{i}\,\|x-y\|_{2},\qquad\forall\,x,y\in G_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{i}(x)-f_{i}(y)|\;\geq\;L_{i}\,\|x-y\|_{2},\qquad\forall\,x,y\in G_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and moreover</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(x)&gt;z_{i},\qquad\forall\,x\in G_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(x)&gt;z_{i},\qquad\forall\,x\in G_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}:=x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}:=x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:=f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:=f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\star}:=\nabla_{x}^{2}f(x^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\star}:=\nabla_{x}^{2}f(x^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. By positive definiteness,
let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}:=\lambda_{\min}(H_{\star})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}:=\lambda_{\min}(H_{\star})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
By continuity of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}f</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}^{\mathrm{H}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}^{\mathrm{H}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}f(x)\;\succeq\;\tfrac{\lambda_{i}}{2}\,I\qquad\text{for all }x\in B(x^{\star},R_{i}^{\mathrm{H}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">⪰</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}f(x)\;\succeq\;\tfrac{\lambda_{i}}{2}\,I\qquad\text{for all }x\in B(x^{\star},R_{i}^{\mathrm{H}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}:=\lambda_{i}/2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}:=\lambda_{i}/2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because the domain is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we could choose a unit vector
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> pointing strictly into the cube at <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is interior,
take any unit vector). Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}\;:=\;\sup\{\,t&gt;0\;:\;x^{\star}+sv_{i}\in[0,1]^{d}\text{ for all }s\in[0,t]\,\}\;&gt;\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}\;:=\;\sup\{\,t&gt;0\;:\;x^{\star}+sv_{i}\in[0,1]^{d}\text{ for all }s\in[0,t]\,\}\;&gt;\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">and set <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}:=\min\{R_{i}^{\mathrm{H}},\,\tau_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}:=\min\{R_{i}^{\mathrm{H}},\,\tau_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:=\min_{1\leq i\leq D}R_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:=\min_{1\leq i\leq D}R_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix any <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,R)</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the restriction</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)\;:=\;f(x^{\star}+tv_{i}),\qquad t\in[0,r]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)\;:=\;f(x^{\star}+tv_{i}),\qquad t\in[0,r].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime\prime}(t)\;=\;v_{i}^{\top}\nabla^{2}f(x^{\star}+tv_{i})\,v_{i}\;\geq\;\mu_{i}\quad\text{for all }t\in[0,r]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime\prime}(t)\;=\;v_{i}^{\top}\nabla^{2}f(x^{\star}+tv_{i})\,v_{i}\;\geq\;\mu_{i}\quad\text{for all }t\in[0,r].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible inward,
we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)\geq g(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)\geq g(0)</annotation></semantics></math> for small <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> leading to the one‑sided derivative
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(0+)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(0+)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is interior then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(x^{\star})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(x^{\star})=0</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>).
Because <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime\prime}\geq\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime\prime}\geq\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the derivative <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing and thus</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(t)\;\geq\;g^{\prime}(0+)+\mu_{i}t\;\geq\;\mu_{i}t,\qquad t\in[0,r]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(t)\;\geq\;g^{\prime}(0+)+\mu_{i}t\;\geq\;\mu_{i}t,\qquad t\in[0,r].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:=r/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:=r/4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:=r/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:=r/2</annotation></semantics></math> and define the segment</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}\;:=\;\{\,x^{\star}+tv_{i}:t\in[a,b]\,\}\;\subset\;B(x^{\star},r)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">⊂</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}\;:=\;\{\,x^{\star}+tv_{i}:t\in[a,b]\,\}\;\subset\;B(x^{\star},r),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">whose length is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}:=b-a=r/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}:=b-a=r/4</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x^{\star}+tv_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x^{\star}+tv_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=x^{\star}+sv_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=x^{\star}+sv_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;s</annotation></semantics></math>, the mean value theorem
gives some <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in(s,t)\subset[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in(s,t)\subset[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f(x)-f(y)|\;=\;|g(t)-g(s)|\;=\;|g^{\prime}(\xi)|\,|t-s|\;\geq\;\mu_{i}a\,|t-s|\;=\;\Bigl(\frac{\lambda_{i}r}{8}\Bigr)\,\|x-y\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.448em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f(x)-f(y)|\;=\;|g(t)-g(s)|\;=\;|g^{\prime}(\xi)|\,|t-s|\;\geq\;\mu_{i}a\,|t-s|\;=\;\Bigl(\frac{\lambda_{i}r}{8}\Bigr)\,\|x-y\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore the choice</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}\;:=\;\frac{\lambda_{i}r}{8}\;&gt;\;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}\;:=\;\frac{\lambda_{i}r}{8}\;&gt;\;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">works uniformly for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The segment <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> does not contain <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all its points are at distance at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=r/4&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=r/4&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By uniqueness of the minimizer, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)&gt;f(x^{\star})=z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)&gt;f(x^{\star})=z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The lemma holds with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}=r/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}=r/4</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}=(\lambda_{\min}(\nabla_{x}^{2}f_{i}(x^{(i)}))\,r)/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}=(\lambda_{\min}(\nabla_{x}^{2}f_{i}(x^{(i)}))\,r)/8</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{1},\dots,z_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{1},\dots,z_{D})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the minima defined above.
Then there exist constants <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following holds:
for any <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and any perturbation <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\delta_{0}|&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\delta_{0}|&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{i}+\delta_{0},\dots,z_{D})-F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{D})\bigr|\;\geq\;L_{0}\,|\delta_{0}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{i}+\delta_{0},\dots,z_{D})-F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{D})\bigr|\;\geq\;L_{0}\,|\delta_{0}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th standard basis vector of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By assumption, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}\coloneqq\bigl|\partial_{i}F_{0}(z)\bigr|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}\coloneqq\bigl|\partial_{i}F_{0}(z)\bigr|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}\in C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}\in C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto\partial_{i}F_{0}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto\partial_{i}F_{0}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous at <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence for each <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\partial_{i}F_{0}(u)\bigr|\;\geq\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{i}\quad\text{whenever}\quad\|u-z\|_{\infty}&lt;r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>whenever</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\partial_{i}F_{0}(u)\bigr|\;\geq\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,m_{i}\quad\text{whenever}\quad\|u-z\|_{\infty}&lt;r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">If necessary, shrink <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}</annotation></semantics></math> so that the line segment
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\,z+te_{i}:|t|&lt;r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\,z+te_{i}:|t|&lt;r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}\,\}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define uniform constants</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}\;\coloneqq\;\tfrac{1}{2}\min_{1\leq i\leq D}m_{i}\;&gt;\;0,\qquad r_{0}\;\coloneqq\;\min_{1\leq i\leq D}r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}\;&gt;\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>cont</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}\;\coloneqq\;\tfrac{1}{2}\min_{1\leq i\leq D}m_{i}\;&gt;\;0,\qquad r_{0}\;\coloneqq\;\min_{1\leq i\leq D}r_{i}^{\mathrm{cont}}\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\delta_{0}|&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\delta_{0}|&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the one-dimensional slice <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(t)\coloneqq F_{0}(z+te_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(t)\coloneqq F_{0}(z+te_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|t|&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|t|&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}^{\prime}(t)=\partial_{i}F_{0}(z+te_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}^{\prime}(t)=\partial_{i}F_{0}(z+te_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the mean value theorem, there exists <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}(z+\delta_{0}e_{i})-F_{0}(z)=g_{i}^{\prime}(\theta\delta_{0})\,\delta_{0}=\partial_{i}F_{0}\!\bigl(z+\theta\delta_{0}e_{i}\bigr)\,\delta_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}(z+\delta_{0}e_{i})-F_{0}(z)=g_{i}^{\prime}(\theta\delta_{0})\,\delta_{0}=\partial_{i}F_{0}\!\bigl(z+\theta\delta_{0}e_{i}\bigr)\,\delta_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking absolute values and using the lower bound on
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\partial_{i}F_{0}(\cdot)\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\partial_{i}F_{0}(\cdot)\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math> inside the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-ball of radius <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
around <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|F_{0}(z+\delta_{0}e_{i})-F_{0}(z)\bigr|\;\geq\;L_{0}\,|\delta_{0}|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|F_{0}(z+\delta_{0}e_{i})-F_{0}(z)\bigr|\;\geq\;L_{0}\,|\delta_{0}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">which is the desired inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmlemma7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=\min_{x\in[0,1]^{d}}f_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\min_{x\in[0,1]^{d}}f_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unique minimizer of <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (as assumed above). Then there exist constants <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The open balls </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B(x^{(i)},R_{0})\}_{i=1}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B(x^{(i)},R_{0})\}_{i=1}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are pairwise disjoint.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and every </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1]^{d}\setminus B(x^{(i)},R_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1]^{d}\setminus B(x^{(i)},R_{0})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(x)\;&gt;\;z_{i}+\varepsilon_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(x)\;&gt;\;z_{i}+\varepsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the minimizers <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct and finite in number, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\;:=\;\min_{i\neq j}\,\bigl\|x^{(i)}-x^{(j)}\bigr\|_{2}\;&gt;\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\;:=\;\min_{i\neq j}\,\bigl\|x^{(i)}-x^{(j)}\bigr\|_{2}\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}:=\tfrac{1}{2}\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}:=\tfrac{1}{2}\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B(x^{(i)},R_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B(x^{(i)},R_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, by the triangle inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-x^{(j)}\|_{2}\;\geq\;\|x^{(i)}-x^{(j)}\|_{2}-\|x-x^{(i)}\|_{2}\;&gt;\;\Delta-R_{0}\;=\;R_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-x^{(j)}\|_{2}\;\geq\;\|x^{(i)}-x^{(j)}\|_{2}-\|x-x^{(i)}\|_{2}\;&gt;\;\Delta-R_{0}\;=\;R_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin B(x^{(j)},R_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin B(x^{(j)},R_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the balls are pairwise disjoint, proving the first part.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second part, fix <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and define the compact set <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}:=[0,1]^{d}\setminus B(x^{(i)},R_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}:=[0,1]^{d}\setminus B(x^{(i)},R_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. The continuity of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that the minimum</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}\;:=\;\min_{x\in K_{i}}f_{i}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}\;:=\;\min_{x\in K_{i}}f_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">is attained on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}\notin K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}\notin K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique global minimizer on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}&gt;z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}&gt;z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}:=m_{i}-z_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}:=m_{i}-z_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and set</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}\;:=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\min_{1\leq i\leq D}\varepsilon_{i}\;&gt;\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}\;:=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\min_{1\leq i\leq D}\varepsilon_{i}\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for every <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(x)\;\geq\;m_{i}\;=\;z_{i}+\varepsilon_{i}\;\geq\;z_{i}+2\varepsilon_{0}\;&gt;\;z_{i}+\varepsilon_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(x)\;\geq\;m_{i}\;=\;z_{i}+\varepsilon_{i}\;\geq\;z_{i}+2\varepsilon_{0}\;&gt;\;z_{i}+\varepsilon_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have proved this lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i2" title="item 2 (2) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (2)</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given the target function under the assumptions. For any given single-layer transformer
defined in the main context, our goal is to find two different sequences such that their output in the part</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Concat}_{i=1}^{h}\Bigl(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sigma\!\left[(W_{K,i}\hat{x}(t))^{\top}W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0}\right]W_{V,i}\hat{x}(t)\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Concat</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Concat}_{i=1}^{h}\Bigl(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sigma\!\left[(W_{K,i}\hat{x}(t))^{\top}W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0}\right]W_{V,i}\hat{x}(t)\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">are very close (differs by only <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\epsilon^{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\epsilon^{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math>), but their output from the target function differs by at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then according to lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have the required parameter count for the FFN <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math> to be at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(1/\epsilon^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(1/\epsilon^{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notations</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,s</annotation></semantics></math>, define the attention weight function</p>
<table id="A1.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}(x,t)\;=\;\exp\!\bigl(\gamma\,(W_{K,i}P_{\phi}(x,t))^{\top}W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}(x,t)\;=\;\exp\!\bigl(\gamma\,(W_{K,i}P_{\phi}(x,t))^{\top}W_{Q,i}\hat{c}_{0}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the value mapping</p>
<table id="A1.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}(x,t)\;=\;W_{V,i}P_{\phi}(x,t)\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}(x,t)\;=\;W_{V,i}P_{\phi}(x,t)\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the softmax scaling factor,
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q,i},W_{K,i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q,i},W_{K,i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times E}</annotation></semantics></math> are the query and key projections,
and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V,i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V,i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the value projection for head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation of sets</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, we assume <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the interior of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the other case can be treated with the same method below.
From lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and lemma <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> we have that there exists <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and segments <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{i}\subset B(x^{(i)},R),i=1,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}\subset B(x^{(i)},R),i=1,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,\delta_{0},r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,\delta_{0},r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x,y\in G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x,y\in G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{i}(x)-f_{i}(y)|&gt;L\|x-y\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{i}(x)-f_{i}(y)|&gt;L\|x-y\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x\in B(x^{(j)},R),y\in B(x^{(i)},R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x\in B(x^{(j)},R),y\in B(x^{(i)},R)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(y)-f_{i}(x)&gt;\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(y)-f_{i}(x)&gt;\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The length of <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i=1,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i=1,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and any perturbation <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\delta_{1}|&lt;\max_{x\in B(x^{(i)},R)}(f_{i}(x)-z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\delta_{1}|&lt;\max_{x\in B(x^{(i)},R)}(f_{i}(x)-z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{i}+\delta_{1},\dots,z_{D})-F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{D})\bigr|\;\geq\;L\,|\delta_{1}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{i}+\delta_{1},\dots,z_{D})-F_{0}(z_{1},\dots,z_{D})\bigr|\;\geq\;L\,|\delta_{1}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{i}:=G_{i}\cup\{x^{(i)}\},i=1,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}:=G_{i}\cup\{x^{(i)}\},i=1,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{0}=\cup_{i=1}^{D}K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}=\cup_{i=1}^{D}K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\frac{\frac{1}{4}T-s-D+1}{(n+1)s+1}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\frac{\frac{1}{4}T-s-D+1}{(n+1)s+1}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume without loss of generality that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{4}T-s-D+1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{4}T-s-D+1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise the result would be trivial.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Max weight for each head</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dots,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dots,s</annotation></semantics></math>, define recursively the pairs <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{j},t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{j},t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<ul id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the first head,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{1},t_{1})\;=\;\arg\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}y\in P_{0}\\
t\in S_{1}\end{subarray}}\,\lambda_{1}(y,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{1},t_{1})\;=\;\arg\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}y\in P_{0}\\
t\in S_{1}\end{subarray}}\,\lambda_{1}(y,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{j},t_{j})\;=\;\arg\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}y\in P_{0}\\
t\in S_{j}\\
t\notin\{t_{1},\dots,t_{j-1}\}\end{subarray}}\,\lambda_{j}(y,t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{j},t_{j})\;=\;\arg\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}y\in P_{0}\\
t\in S_{j}\\
t\notin\{t_{1},\dots,t_{j-1}\}\end{subarray}}\,\lambda_{j}(y,t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If maximum can be obtained at multiple <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,t)</annotation></semantics></math>, then choose one of them.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=\{y_{1},\dots,y_{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=\{y_{1},\dots,y_{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the sets <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1},\dots,K_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1},\dots,K_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise disjoint and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;D</annotation></semantics></math>,
there exists at least one index <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}\,\cap\,Y\;=\;\varnothing." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">∩</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}\,\cap\,Y\;=\;\varnothing.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, we assume that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math>. As we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|S_{i}|\geq\frac{1}{4}T&gt;s+D-1,i=1,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{i}|\geq\frac{1}{4}T&gt;s+D-1,i=1,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that there exists a set of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t^{*}_{2},\dots,t^{*}_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t^{*}_{2},\dots,t^{*}_{D})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<ul id="A1.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}_{j}\notin\{t_{1},\dots,t_{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}_{j}\notin\{t_{1},\dots,t_{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=2,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=2,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t^{*}_{j}\in S_{j},j=2,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}_{j}\in S_{j},j=2,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}=\frac{1}{4}T-s-D+1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}=\frac{1}{4}T-s-D+1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a integer. Then we have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{1}-\{t_{1},\dots,t_{s},t^{*}_{2},\dots,t^{*}_{D}\}|\geq T_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{1}-\{t_{1},\dots,t_{s},t^{*}_{2},\dots,t^{*}_{D}\}|\geq T_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, suppose <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,\dots,T_{0}\}\subset S_{1}-\{t_{1},\dots,t_{s},t^{*}_{2},\dots,t^{*}_{D}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,\dots,T_{0}\}\subset S_{1}-\{t_{1},\dots,t_{s},t^{*}_{2},\dots,t^{*}_{D}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sequences to be considered</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a segment of length <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then it is natural to assign coordinate system <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:[0,1]\to G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:[0,1]\to G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:=f_{1}\circ\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:=f_{1}\circ\eta</annotation></semantics></math> being a monotonically increasing function on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The monotone property is as a result of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{1}(x)-f_{1}(y)|\geq L\|x-y\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{1}(x)-f_{1}(y)|\geq L\|x-y\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">We denote by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=T_{0}\lfloor\frac{rL^{2}}{3T_{0}\epsilon}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=T_{0}\lfloor\frac{rL^{2}}{3T_{0}\epsilon}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}|M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}|M</annotation></semantics></math>, Construct the following <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> sets:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle U_{j}=\frac{j-1}{T_{0}}+\{\frac{1}{M},\dots,\frac{(\frac{T_{0}}{M})}{M}\},j=1,\dots,T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{j}=\frac{j-1}{T_{0}}+\{\frac{1}{M},\dots,\frac{(\frac{T_{0}}{M})}{M}\},j=1,\dots,T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We have <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{j}|=\lfloor\frac{rL^{2}}{3T_{0}\epsilon}\rfloor=O(1/\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{j}|=\lfloor\frac{rL^{2}}{3T_{0}\epsilon}\rfloor=O(1/\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Claim 2.1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Existence of two distinct sub-sequence 
<br class="ltx_break">There exists two subsequences <math id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}(1),\dots,z_{1}(T_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}(1),\dots,z_{1}(T_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{2}(1),\dots z_{2}(T_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{2}(1),\dots z_{2}(T_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}(t)\in\eta(U_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}(t)\in\eta(U_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following conditions.</p>
<ul id="A1.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)}{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)}-\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)v_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)}{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)}\right\|_{2}\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{3T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)}{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)}-\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)v_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)}{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)}\right\|_{2}\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{3T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A1.I6.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,s</annotation></semantics></math>, either of the following holds:</p>
<ol id="A1.I6.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)}{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)}\in\left[1/(1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}),\,1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)}{\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{2}(t),t)}\in\left[1/(1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}),\,1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j=1,2}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{j}(t),t)\leq\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{4}\sum_{w=1}^{s}\lambda_{i}(y_{w},t_{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j=1,2}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{j}(t),t)\leq\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{4}\sum_{w=1}^{s}\lambda_{i}(y_{w},t_{w})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We compare the orders of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> appearing on both sides of the conditions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{t}|=O(1/\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{t}|=O(1/\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the total number of possible
choices of subsequences <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z(1),\dots,z(T_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z(1),\dots,z(T_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\epsilon^{T_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\epsilon^{T_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, to satisfy condition (1), note that both vectors involved are
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional with norms bounded by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the discretization required to
achieve accuracy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{k+1}/(3T_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{k+1}/(3T_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm leads to at most
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\epsilon^{(k+1)ns})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\epsilon^{(k+1)ns})</annotation></semantics></math> distinct possibilities, since there are <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> heads.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For condition (2), observe that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w=1}^{s}\lambda_{i}(y_{w},t_{w})\;\geq\;\tfrac{1}{T_{0}}\max_{j=1,2}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{j}(t),t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w=1}^{s}\lambda_{i}(y_{w},t_{w})\;\geq\;\tfrac{1}{T_{0}}\max_{j=1,2}\sum_{t=1}^{T_{0}}\lambda_{i}(z_{j}(t),t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, for each <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the relevant interval can be partitioned into at most
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\left(\tfrac{-\log\epsilon}{\epsilon^{k+1}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\left(\tfrac{-\log\epsilon}{\epsilon^{k+1}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> sub-intervals.
Taken across <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> heads, this contributes at most
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\left((-\log\epsilon)^{s}/\epsilon^{(k+1)s}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\left((-\log\epsilon)^{s}/\epsilon^{(k+1)s}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> possibilities.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two conditions, the total number of distinct admissible cases is
bounded above by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\left(\frac{(-\log\epsilon)^{s}}{\epsilon^{(k+1)ns+(k+1)s}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\left(\frac{(-\log\epsilon)^{s}}{\epsilon^{(k+1)ns+(k+1)s}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}\geq(k+1)ns+(k+1)s+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}\geq(k+1)ns+(k+1)s+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\left(\frac{1}{\epsilon^{T_{0}}}\right)\;\gg\;O\!\left(\frac{(-\log\epsilon)^{s}}{\epsilon^{(k+1)ns+(k+1)s}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≫</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\left(\frac{1}{\epsilon^{T_{0}}}\right)\;\gg\;O\!\left(\frac{(-\log\epsilon)^{s}}{\epsilon^{(k+1)ns+(k+1)s}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by the pigeonhole principle, there must exist two distinct subsequences
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{1}(1),\dots,z_{1}(T_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{1}(1),\dots,z_{1}(T_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{2}(1),\dots,z_{2}(T_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{2}(1),\dots,z_{2}(T_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying all the
conditions of Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1" title="Claim 2.1. ‣ Sequences to be considered ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Construction of Distinct sequences</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1" title="Claim 2.1. ‣ Sequences to be considered ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, we have constructed two sub-sequences <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the given conditions. We now consider the construction of two full input sequence <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}(t)=z_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}(t)=z_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}(t)=w_{2}(t)=x^{(D)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}(t)=w_{2}(t)=x^{(D)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Otherwise, <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}(t)=z_{1}(t),w_{2}(t)=z_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}(t)=z_{1}(t),w_{2}(t)=z_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}(t_{i})=y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}(t_{i})=y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,s;\quad j=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,s;\quad j=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}(t^{*}_{i})=x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}(t^{*}_{i})=x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I7.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2,\dots,D;\quad j=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2,\dots,D;\quad j=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all other <math id="A1.I7.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I7.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}(t)=x^{(D)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}(t)=x^{(D)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Difference of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W1,W2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W1,W2</annotation></semantics></math> applied to target function</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Denote by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of all indices <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}(t)\neq z_{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}(t)\neq z_{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}=[T_{0}]-I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}=[T_{0}]-I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{3}=[T]-I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{3}=[T]-I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is clear from the difference of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}\neq\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}\neq\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">We then define the following notations for the simplicity of calculation (defined for each head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,s</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<ul id="A1.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{1,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{1,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{2,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{2}(t),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{2,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{2}(t),t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(w_{1}(t),t))/Q_{1,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(w_{1}(t),t))/Q_{1,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{2,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{2}(t),t)v_{i}(w_{2}(t),t))/Q_{2,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{2,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{1}}\lambda_{i}(w_{2}(t),t)v_{i}(w_{2}(t),t))/Q_{2,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{3,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{2}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{3,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{2}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is also the same if defined on <math id="A1.I8.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{3,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{2}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(z_{1}(t),t))/Q_{3,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{3,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{2}}\lambda_{i}(z_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(z_{1}(t),t))/Q_{3,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the same if defined on <math id="A1.I8.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I8.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{4,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{3}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{4,i}=\sum_{t\in I_{3}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the same if defined on <math id="A1.I8.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I8.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{4,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{3}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(w_{1}(t),t))/Q_{4,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{4,i}=(\sum_{t\in I_{3}}\lambda_{i}(w_{1}(t),t)v_{i}(w_{1}(t),t))/Q_{4,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the same if defined on <math id="A1.I8.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}()</annotation></semantics></math> maps to positive values, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{j,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{j,i}</annotation></semantics></math> are convex combinations of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}()</annotation></semantics></math>, whose norm is bounded by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> according to the constraint section <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Model constraints). ‣ Assumptions on the target class ‣ 4 Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Therefore <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|V_{j,i}\|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|V_{j,i}\|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,2,3,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,2,3,4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}\circ\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}\circ\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{t}=\max_{t\in I_{1}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{t}=\max_{t\in I_{1}}t</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</p>
<ul id="A1.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t\in S_{1}}f_{1}(w_{1}(t))=f_{1}(w_{1}(\tilde{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t\in S_{1}}f_{1}(w_{1}(t))=f_{1}(w_{1}(\tilde{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t\in S_{1}}f_{1}(w_{2}(t))=f_{1}(w_{2}(\tilde{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t\in S_{1}}f_{1}(w_{2}(t))=f_{1}(w_{2}(\tilde{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">And by construction we know that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(w_{1}(\tilde{t}))-(w_{2}(\tilde{t}))\|\geq\frac{r}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(w_{1}(\tilde{t}))-(w_{2}(\tilde{t}))\|\geq\frac{r}{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which is the minimal distance for any two points in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\tilde{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\tilde{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|f_{1}(w_{1}(\tilde{t}))-f_{1}(w_{2}(\tilde{t}))|\geq\frac{rL}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|f_{1}(w_{1}(\tilde{t}))-f_{1}(w_{2}(\tilde{t}))|\geq\frac{rL}{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.4" class="ltx_p">As we have for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<ul id="A1.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(w_{1}(t))=z^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(w_{1}(t))=z^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(w_{2}(t))=z^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t\in S_{i}}f_{i}(w_{2}(t))=z^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Then following the perturbation property of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> defined above we have that the difference of output between the two sequence to be at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{rL^{2}}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{rL^{2}}{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is greater than <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation requires that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px7.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Model(W_{1})-Model(W_{2})|\geq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Model(W_{1})-Model(W_{2})|\geq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are close after attention layer</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any given head <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the the two cases given in <a href="#Thmtheorem2.Thmclaim1" title="Claim 2.1. ‣ Sequences to be considered ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Case 1 can be rewritten as follows:</p>
<ul id="A1.I11" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I11.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\frac{Q_{1,i}V_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}-\frac{Q_{2,i}V_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}}\|_{2}\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{3T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\frac{Q_{1,i}V_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}-\frac{Q_{2,i}V_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}}\|_{2}\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{3T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I11.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}{Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}}\in\left[1/(1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}),\,1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}{Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}}\in\left[1/(1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}),\,1+\tfrac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{12T_{0}^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, we assume <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{1,i}\geq Q_{2,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{1,i}\geq Q_{2,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By calculation, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Q_{1,i}V_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}-\frac{Q_{2,i}V_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Q_{1,i}V_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}-\frac{Q_{2,i}V_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}V_{3,i}}{Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Q_{3,i}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{3,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i})(Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i})}+\frac{Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Q_{3,i}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{3,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i})(Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i})}+\frac{Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We have already known that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{4,i}\geq\frac{Q_{1,i}+Q_{2,i}}{T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{4,i}\geq\frac{Q_{1,i}+Q_{2,i}}{T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{4,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{4,i}</annotation></semantics></math> has the max weight of each head in it). Then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{4,i}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{4,i})(Q_{2,i}+Q_{4,i})}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{4,i}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{4,i})(Q_{2,i}+Q_{4,i})}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{4,i})}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{4,i})}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{T_{0}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i})}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{T_{0}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i})}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{T_{0}\epsilon^{k+1}(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{12T_{0}^{2}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{T_{0}\epsilon^{k+1}(V_{4,i}-V_{2,i})}{12T_{0}^{2}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{6T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{6T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we also have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{3,i}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{3,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i})(Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i})}\|\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{6T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{3,i}(Q_{2,i}-Q_{1,i})(V_{3,i}-V_{2,i})}{(Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i})(Q_{2,i}+Q_{3,i})}\|\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{6T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.5" class="ltx_p">From inequality <a href="#A1.E26" title="In Case 1 ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> and substituting equation <a href="#A1.E24" title="In Case 1 ‣ A.2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})\|\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{6T_{0}}+\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{3T_{0}}=\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{2T_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})\|\leq\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{6T_{0}}+\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{3T_{0}}=\frac{\epsilon^{k+1}}{2T_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.Px9.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{4,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{4,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\frac{T_{0}Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\frac{T_{0}Q_{1,i}}{Q_{1,i}+Q_{3,i}}(V_{1,i}-V_{2,i})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
