</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">By construction,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x)=p_{3}\,\sigma\!\Bigl(Q_{3}\bigl(C_{2}\,\sigma(D_{2}\,\sigma(E_{2}(A_{1}\,\sigma(B_{1}x+b_{1})+a_{1})+e_{2})+d_{2})+c_{2}\bigr)+q_{3}\Bigr)+r_{3}=F_{3}\!\bigl(F_{2}\!\bigl(F_{1}(x)\bigr)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x)=p_{3}\,\sigma\!\Bigl(Q_{3}\bigl(C_{2}\,\sigma(D_{2}\,\sigma(E_{2}(A_{1}\,\sigma(B_{1}x+b_{1})+a_{1})+e_{2})+d_{2})+c_{2}\bigr)+q_{3}\Bigr)+r_{3}=F_{3}\!\bigl(F_{2}\!\bigl(F_{1}(x)\bigr)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> realizes the composition exactly, has <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> hidden layers (hence <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> layers total),
and its hidden widths are precisely those of the constituent hidden layers of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmlemma9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Approximating <math id="Thmlemma9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max</annotation></semantics></math> with a shallow ReLU network)<span id="Thmlemma9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]^{T}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]^{T}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{1},\dots,x_{T})=\max\{x_{1},\dots,x_{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{1},\dots,x_{T})=\max\{x_{1},\dots,x_{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a fully connected ReLU network <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<em id="Thmlemma9.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">three layers</em> (i.e., two hidden layers and one output layer), whose hidden-layer widths are each at most
<math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2T\,\lceil 1/\epsilon\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2T\,\lceil 1/\epsilon\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, such that
<math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximates <math id="Thmlemma9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Approximating max with a shallow ReLU network). ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>
Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\lceil 1/\epsilon\rceil." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\lceil 1/\epsilon\rceil.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each coordinate <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math> and each grid index <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,1,\dots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0,1,\dots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
define the first hidden layer neurons by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(t,i)\;=\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(x_{t}-\tfrac{i}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(t,i)\;=\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(x_{t}-\tfrac{i}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,1,\dots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,1,\dots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, define the second hidden layer neurons by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(j)\;=\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}h_{1}(t,j)\right)-\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}h_{1}(t,j)-\tfrac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(j)\;=\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}h_{1}(t,j)\right)-\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}h_{1}(t,j)-\tfrac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the output of the network is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x_{1},\dots,x_{T})\;=\;\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}h_{2}(j)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x_{1},\dots,x_{T})\;=\;\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}h_{2}(j).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Claim.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,\dots,n-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,\dots,n-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and set</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T}h_{1}(t,j)\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T}\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\frac{j}{n}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T}h_{1}(t,j)\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T}\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\frac{j}{n}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(j)\;=\;\operatorname{ReLU}(S_{j})\;-\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(S_{j}-\frac{1}{n}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(j)\;=\;\operatorname{ReLU}(S_{j})\;-\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(S_{j}-\frac{1}{n}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">1) If <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(j)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(j)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then necessarily <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ReLU}(z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ReLU}(z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), hence there exists some <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\tfrac{j}{n}\Big)&gt;0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad x_{t}&gt;\tfrac{j}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\tfrac{j}{n}\Big)&gt;0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad x_{t}&gt;\tfrac{j}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(j)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(j)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> only if <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\,t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}&gt;j/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}&gt;j/n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">2) If there exists <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}&gt;(j+1)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}&gt;(j+1)/n</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}\;\geq\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\tfrac{j}{n}\Big)\;&gt;\;\tfrac{1}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}\;\geq\;\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\tfrac{j}{n}\Big)\;&gt;\;\tfrac{1}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}\geq\tfrac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}\geq\tfrac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we get</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(j)\;=\;S_{j}-\Big(S_{j}-\tfrac{1}{n}\Big)\;=\;\tfrac{1}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(j)\;=\;S_{j}-\Big(S_{j}-\tfrac{1}{n}\Big)\;=\;\tfrac{1}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t}x_{t}\in(j/n,(j+1)/n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t}x_{t}\in(j/n,(j+1)/n]</annotation></semantics></math>.
By construction,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(k)=0\quad\text{for }k\geq j+1,\qquad h_{2}(k)=\tfrac{1}{n}\quad\text{for }k\leq j-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(k)=0\quad\text{for }k\geq j+1,\qquad h_{2}(k)=\tfrac{1}{n}\quad\text{for }k\leq j-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">and for <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=j</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\;\leq\;h_{2}(j)=\operatorname{ReLU}(S_{j})-\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(S_{j}-\tfrac{1}{n}\Big)\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{n},\quad S_{j}:=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\tfrac{j}{n}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.535em;" width="2.535em"><mi>ReLU</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\;\leq\;h_{2}(j)=\operatorname{ReLU}(S_{j})-\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(S_{j}-\tfrac{1}{n}\Big)\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{n},\quad S_{j}:=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\operatorname{ReLU}\!\Big(x_{t}-\tfrac{j}{n}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}h_{2}(k)=\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\tfrac{1}{n}+h_{2}(j)\in\Big[\tfrac{j}{n},\,\tfrac{j}{n}+\tfrac{1}{n}\Big]=\Big[\tfrac{j}{n},\,\tfrac{j+1}{n}\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}h_{2}(k)=\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\tfrac{1}{n}+h_{2}(j)\in\Big[\tfrac{j}{n},\,\tfrac{j}{n}+\tfrac{1}{n}\Big]=\Big[\tfrac{j}{n},\,\tfrac{j+1}{n}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{t}x_{t}\in(j/n,(j+1)/n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{t}x_{t}\in(j/n,(j+1)/n]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\;\leq\;|\hat{f}(x)-\max_{t}x_{t}|\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{n}\;\leq\;\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\;\leq\;|\hat{f}(x)-\max_{t}x_{t}|\;\leq\;\tfrac{1}{n}\;\leq\;\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximates <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\max_{t}x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\max_{t}x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#S5.I1.i3" title="item 2 (3) ‣ Theorem 2 (Approximation rates of transformers). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2 (3)</span></a>
<br class="ltx_break">We begin by fixing the embedding with positional information.
Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}:[0,1]^{d}\times[T]\to\mathbb{R}^{dT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}:[0,1]^{d}\times[T]\to\mathbb{R}^{dT}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}(x(t),t)=(0,\dots,0,\,x(t),\,0,\dots,0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}(x(t),t)=(0,\dots,0,\,x(t),\,0,\dots,0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the vector <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> occupies the <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th block of dimension <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, and all
other blocks are zero. With the classification token <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the
attention layer reduces to a trivial aggregation, and the output (prior to the
feed-forward network) is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{T}\,(x(1),\dots,x(T))\in[0,1]^{dT}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{T}\,(x(1),\dots,x(T))\in[0,1]^{dT}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Given a target accuracy <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct three feed-forward networks
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1},F_{2},F_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1},F_{2},F_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Approximating the component functions.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}:\tfrac{1}{T}[0,1]^{d\times T}\;\to\;\mathbb{R}^{D\times T},\qquad F_{1}\bigl(\tfrac{1}{T}x(1),\dots,\tfrac{1}{T}x(T)\bigr)=(u(1),\dots,u(T))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}:\tfrac{1}{T}[0,1]^{d\times T}\;\to\;\mathbb{R}^{D\times T},\qquad F_{1}\bigl(\tfrac{1}{T}x(1),\dots,\tfrac{1}{T}x(T)\bigr)=(u(1),\dots,u(T)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u(t)_{i}-f_{i}(x(t))|\leq\epsilon\quad\text{for all }i=1,\dots,D." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u(t)_{i}-f_{i}(x(t))|\leq\epsilon\quad\text{for all }i=1,\dots,D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Approximation of components). ‣ 5 Approximation rate of Generalized 𝐷-Retrieval Tasks ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, such an approximation can be
implemented by a two-layer FFN with parameter count
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\epsilon^{\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\epsilon^{\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Approximating the minimization.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}^{\prime}:\mathbb{R}^{D\times T}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}^{\prime}:\mathbb{R}^{D\times T}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}^{\prime}(u(1),\dots,u(T))=(u_{1},\dots,u_{D}),\qquad u_{i}=\min_{t\in S_{i}}u(t)_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}^{\prime}(u(1),\dots,u(T))=(u_{1},\dots,u_{D}),\qquad u_{i}=\min_{t\in S_{i}}u(t)_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Approximating max with a shallow ReLU network). ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> (which works the same for taking minimum), there exists a three-layer ReLU network with
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> parameters that <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximates <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We denote this approximation by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Approximating the outer function.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{3}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{3}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a two-layer FFN that
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximates <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, with parameter count <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\epsilon^{\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\epsilon^{\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Composition.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on a compact domain, it is Lipschitz with constant <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min</annotation></semantics></math> operator is 1-Lipschitz. Therefore, the composed network</p>
<table id="A1.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{3}\circ F_{2}\circ F_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{3}\circ F_{2}\circ F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">provides an <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of the target function, with total
parameter count</p>
<table id="A1.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\epsilon^{\gamma+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\epsilon^{\gamma+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">According to lemma <a href="#Thmlemma8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ Proof Sketch. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Main Theorems ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{3}\circ F_{2}\circ F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{3}\circ F_{2}\circ F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written equivalently as a five-layer FFN.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Details for Experiment 1</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.1 </span>Experimental details for Section <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Numerical verification of Theorem with synthetic dataset ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a></h4>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data generation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The intrinsic dimension of the synthetic task is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=4</annotation></semantics></math>. For each sequence length
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\{8,16,32,64,128\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\{8,16,32,64,128\}</annotation></semantics></math> we generate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8000</annotation></semantics></math> training and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> validation
examples. The inputs are i.i.d. Gaussian samples <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{4})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model architecture.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each input vector <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is first mapped to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{8h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{8h}</annotation></semantics></math> by a two-layer
feed-forward network with hidden dimension <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and ReLU activations, ensuring
a per-head embedding dimension of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>. A trainable classification token <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
is appended, and no positional encoding is used since the task is permutation
invariant. The sequence is processed by a single-layer multi-head attention
block without residual connections or layer normalization, consistent with the
theoretical setting. The output is concatenated and passed through a two-layer
GeLU-activated feed-forward network with hidden dimension <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the
final scalar prediction. The fixed hidden size ensures comparability of
parameter counts across different <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training protocol.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each configuration <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,T)</annotation></semantics></math> is trained separately under multiple random seeds.
To reduce the effect of optimization variance, we report the <em id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">minimal
validation error</em> achieved across seeds. This choice isolates expressivity
limitations of the architecture from randomness in training dynamics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation metric.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the normalized mean squared error (NMSE), defined as mean squared error
divided by the variance of the targets. As <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> increases, maxima of Gaussian
samples concentrate, shrinking target variance and making trivial predictors
appear competitive under raw MSE. Normalization by variance corrects this effect
and ensures comparability across lengths. NMSE is also equivalent to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard coefficient of determination.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variance across seeds.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While mean performance across seeds is also informative, reporting the minimal
validation NMSE highlights the best achievable accuracy for a given
architecture. This emphasizes limitations due to model capacity rather than
training noise. Tables showing seed variance are included for completeness (Table <a href="#A2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ B.1.2 Figures and Tables for Synthetic Experiment ‣ B.1 Details for Experiment 1 ‣ Appendix B Experiment Details ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.2 </span>Figures and Tables for Synthetic Experiment <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Numerical verification of Theorem with synthetic dataset ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a></h4>

<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06662v1/toy_remark.svg" id="A2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:329/245;" width="329" height="245"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>A zoom in plot of Figure<a href="#S6.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 6.1 Numerical verification of Theorem with synthetic dataset ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, which shows that when the number of head is enough, the loss first decreases and then increases, as explained in the remark <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Numerical verification of Theorem with synthetic dataset ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.06662v1/nmse_vs_hidden_1.svg" id="A2.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/198;" width="548" height="198"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span> Additional plot of <a href="#S6.F1.sf2" title="In Figure 1 ‣ 6.1 Numerical verification of Theorem with synthetic dataset ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ The Effect of Attention Head Count on Transformer Approximation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(b)</span></a> for <math id="A2.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=2</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
